## 🌐 VMware Networking

The ESXi environment currently uses standard vSphere virtual switches.

### KLMESX01

- `vSwitch0`
  - Management Network
  - VM Network
  - `vmnic0` uplink

- `vSwitch1`
  - Private Lab Switch-LAN
  - No physical uplink currently configured

- `vSwitch-vMotion`
  - VMkernel-vMotion
  - `vmnic1` uplink

### KLMESX02

- `vSwitch0`
  - Management Network
  - VM Network
  - `vmnic0` uplink

- `vSwitch1`
  - Private Lab Switch-LAN

The environment currently uses untagged VLAN configuration for the documented port groups.

The **Private Lab Switch-LAN** is used to provide an isolated virtual networking environment for laboratory workloads.

